  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given an array AAA of length NNN. You can perform the following operation on it:\n\n\nChoose two indices iii and jjj (1≤i&lt;j≤∣A∣1 \\leq i \\lt j \\leq |A|1≤i&lt;j≤∣A∣) such that Ai=AjA_i = A_jAi​=Aj​.\nDelete both AiA_iAi​ and AjA_jAj​ from AAA, and append ∣Ai−Aj∣|A_i - A_j|∣Ai​−Aj​∣ to AAA.\n\nThe length of the array reduces by 111, and all remaining elements are re-indexed to start from 111.\nFind the **minimum** possible length of AAA after performing this operation several (possibly, zero) times.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN, denoting the length of AAA.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ — the elements of AAA.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line a single integer: the minimum possible length of AAA after performing the given operation several times.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "0≤Ai≤N0 \\leq A_i \\leq N0≤Ai​≤N",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n4\n3 1 4 2\n2\n1 1\n3\n1 1 0",
        "output": "4\n1\n1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : There are no deletions we can do. Hence, the answer is 444, the size of the initial array.\nTest Case 2 : We can choose i=1,j=2i = 1, j = 2i=1,j=2. Note that A1=A2=1A_1 = A_2 = 1A1​=A2​=1, and then insert their difference 000 back into the array while deleting the 111s. Thus, the final array becomes [0][0][0] of size 111."
      }
    ]
